@nsobid-F19B2E01E1794F933A9720C1404BB6F6

# Bayonetta 2 1.2 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// The graphics init builds its nn::gfx SwapChainInfo with a buffer count of
// 3, and the NVN window is created with that many textures. Using 2 instead
// lets the CPU run at most one frame ahead of scanout, cutting a frame of
// input latency. The scan buffer view arrays are filled up to the real
// count and read through the acquired texture index, so their unused third
// entry is never touched. The separate 3-slot fence ring is left as is.

@enabled
00DC2454 48008052   // MOV W8,#2 for SwapChainInfo buffer count (was MOV W8,#3)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Bayonetta 2 1.2 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_010, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
